  "body": "I don't know any `Element` that is not `HTMLElement` nor `SVGElement`. I propose:\r\n\r\n1. If we have one, it would be helpful to describe the exception here: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#htmlorsvgelement\r\n2. If not, convert it as a `partial interface Element` so that TypeScript users can be happy in the following example:\r\n\r\n   ```ts\r\n   const elements = document.querySelector(\"[data-cite]\");\r\n   elements[0].dataset; // Error: Property 'dataset' does not exist on type 'Element'.\r\n   ```",
